   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Firefighter Tim Gunther Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8755",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8755-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-l, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8755\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Firefighter Tim Gunther Memorial High-\nway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo honor the life and service of fallen firefighter, Tim Gunther, by\ndesignating a portion of Route, 55 in Poughkeepsie in his memory.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law to designate the portion of Route 55\nin the city of Poughkeepsie as \"Firefighter Tim Gunther Memorial High-\nway.\"\n\nSection 2: Provides that the Commissioner of Transportation shall\nprovide for the installation and maintenance of the ceremonial signage.\n\nSection 3: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation comes at the request of the City of Poughkeepsie, and\nwould honor Tim Gunther, a 21-year veteran of the City of Poughkeepsie\nFire Department. Tragically, on May 4, 2015 Firefighter Gunther made the\nultimate sacrifice when he died of cardiac-related issues after coura-\ngeously battling a fatal fire at a home on Poughkeepsie's Church Street.\n\nIn addition to his career as a celebrated member of the City of Pough-\nkeepsie Fire Department, Gunther, a lifelong resident of the Hudson\nValley, remained actively involved in the local community throughout his\nlife. Gunther was the recipient of numerous awards and accolades, both\nin and out of the department that celebrated his dedication, heroism and\ncompassion. In 2015, Gunther was posthumously awarded the states highest\nhonor for his service, the Liberty Medal.\n\nDesignating a portion of Route 55 in his memory is one way the community\nwill be able to ensure that his legacy lives on and continues to inspire\nboth residents and visitors alike.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: A similar bill (S.5993) passed the Senate unanimously\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
